/**
 * Get PnL metrics aggregated by sub-team.

Reads sub-team membership from the DuckDB mart table, then calculates
PnL metrics per sub-team. Per the AS5 PRD (Feature 2), each request
takes a single ``benchmark_id`` (default: XBI) which drives the
values in the single ``alpha`` column. The card's UI dropdown is
what changes ``benchmark_id``; the column header stays fixed as
``"alpha"`` regardless of selection.

Sub-team attribution uses **current composition only** — only
active members contribute to PnL. Former members are excluded from
both attribution and the response (the card surfaces no greyed-out
rows for them).

The response is a flat list of one row per sub-team, sorted by the
requested metric. Each row carries the team-lead and team-members
avatars plus the team's PnL metrics and a single ``alpha`` column.

## Example Request

```json
{
    "date_range": {"start_date": "2026-01-01", "end_date": "2026-04-14"},
    "filters": {},
    "benchmark_id": "XBI US Equity"
}
```

Omitting ``benchmark_id`` falls back to the PRD default
(``"XBI US Equity"``).

## Example Response

```json
{
    "data": [
        {
            "team_lead_avatar": "analyst@example.test|Jane|Smith",
            "team_members_avatars": "analyst@example.test|Jane|Smith,analyst@example.test|John|Doe",
            "average_net_exposure": 150000000,
            "cumulative_group_pnl_percent": 0.045,
            "alpha": 0.023,
            "cumulative_pnl_percent_nav": 0.012,
            "cumulative_pnl": 5400000
        }
    ],
    "metadata": {
        "date_range": {"start_date": "2026-01-01", "end_date": "2026-04-14"},
        "filters": null,
        "group_by": ["team_lead_avatar"],
        "sort": {"sort_by": ["average_net_exposure"], "sort_descending": true},
        "record_count": 1,
        "display_columns": [
            "team_lead_avatar", "team_members_avatars",
            "average_net_exposure", "cumulative_group_pnl_percent",
            "alpha", "cumulative_pnl_percent_nav", "cumulative_pnl"
        ]
    }
}
```

The ``alpha`` value is the alpha against whichever benchmark was
passed as ``benchmark_id`` — switching the dropdown re-issues the
request and the same column header reports the new benchmark's
alpha.
 * @summary Get Pnl By Subteam Stats Endpoint
 */
